          "message": {
            "text": "The default/legacy A/B proves this oracle exercises shaped-cluster fallback rather than merely producing a plausible green report. On macOS with Chromium 147, the default arm reports 8 agreements, 0 mismatches, and 1 explicit known skip; DOMOTIONCLUSTERFALLBACK=0 reports exactly 4 mismatches—the four mid-cluster cases named here—plus the same skip. The focused reconciliation tests, full unit suite, build, and lint also pass.",
            "markdown": "The default/legacy A/B proves this oracle exercises shaped-cluster fallback rather than merely producing a plausible green report. On macOS with Chromium 147, the default arm reports 8 agreements, 0 mismatches, and 1 explicit known skip; `DOMOTION_CLUSTER_FALLBACK=0` reports exactly 4 mismatches—the four mid-cluster cases named here—plus the same skip. The focused reconciliation tests, full unit suite, build, and lint also pass."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "tools/cluster-conformance.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 43,
                  "endLine": 50,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": " * Discrimination (the requirement that makes the instrument worth its exit code):\n * the shaped-cluster mechanism is shipped default-on and agrees on every\n * currently comparable cell, so a DEFAULT run is GREEN. Toggling\n * `DOMOTION_CLUSTER_FALLBACK=0` restores the legacy per-codepoint walk and this\n * oracle then reads RED on exactly the\n * cells the mechanism fixes (x+U+0951, ก+U+0301, Arial ل+U+08F0, Menlo α+U+0345).\n * That A/B is the proof the instrument discriminates; see docs/113 §2 and the\n * per-cell table in the ticket notes."
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
